<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore May M1 rises 5.6 pct yr on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore May M1 rises 5.6 pct yr on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>			     May 97   April 97   May 96   April 96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	27.58    27.67	26.11    26.49</p>
<p>M-2			  118.91   118.22     106.88   105.81</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	147.22   146.97     133.06   132.25</p>
<p>Demand deposits	   16.96    17.05	16.11    16.43</p>
<p>Currency in active	10.63    10.62	10.01    10.06</p>
<p>circulation</p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 5.6 percent year-on-year in May, compared with 4.4 percent in April.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
